WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.012
Welcome to the Concilium Security Risk Brief for Tuesday, October twenty seventh.

2
00:00:05.012 --> 00:00:12.874
Five minutes of security coverage from the last twenty four hours, to increase your situational awareness without decreasing your productivity.

3
00:00:12.874 --> 00:00:16.214
Here's what matters today.

4
00:00:16.214 --> 00:00:17.584
We start in Ethiopia.

5
00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:26.941
BBC Africa and Reuters report that more than sixty people were killed in attacks on Christians in the Oromia region over the past week, according to the Ethiopian Orthodox Church.

6
00:00:26.941 --> 00:00:37.424
A local official blamed a new rebel coalition that includes the Oromo Liberation Army, which has not commented and has denied carrying out previous such attacks.

7
00:00:37.424 --> 00:00:38.522
Separately, the U.K.

8
00:00:38.522 --> 00:00:46.453
Foreign Office updated its Ethiopia travel advice yesterday with new information about increased tensions and armed groups.

9
00:00:46.453 --> 00:00:55.851
In the Middle East, Reuters reports Jordan carried out airstrikes in southern Syria after linking the attackers in the recent attack on a church in Jordan to terrorist groups.

10
00:00:55.851 --> 00:01:02.893
Dawn, citing health officials in Syria's Daraa province, reports six people were killed, including three children and a woman.

11
00:01:02.893 --> 00:01:16.731
Syria's border and customs authority then closed the Nassib border crossing with Jordan, suspending passenger and commercial traffic in both directions from today, according to its statement carried by C G T N Europe.

12
00:01:16.731 --> 00:01:22.819
In Saudi Arabia, Reuters reports the Saudi led coalition says it intercepted Houthi missiles and drones attacking the kingdom.

13
00:01:22.819 --> 00:01:32.903
The Express Tribune, citing Bloomberg News, reports Saudi Arabia contained a fire near its Ras Tanura oil export terminal early today after an attack in the region.

14
00:01:32.903 --> 00:01:37.497
And Reuters reports Egypt has approved military support for Saudi Arabia.

15
00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:45.085
In the Democratic Republic of the Congo, Reuters reports Ebola infections have passed ten thousand, according to the government.

16
00:01:45.085 --> 00:01:50.484
Reuters also reports protesters killed a longtime nurse who was treating Ebola patients.

17
00:01:50.484 --> 00:02:01.919
In Sudan, a drone strike on a market in Nyala, in Darfur, killed twenty one people and wounded at least forty, a medical source and witnesses told A F P, as reported by Dawn.

18
00:02:01.919 --> 00:02:07.969
Reuters reports drone strikes also cut power across southeast Sudan, the power operator says.

19
00:02:07.969 --> 00:02:10.351
A few updates on stories we've covered.

20
00:02:10.351 --> 00:02:17.534
In Nigeria, police told BBC Africa the death toll from the attack in Taraba State has risen to at least forty eight.

21
00:02:17.534 --> 00:02:26.375
In India, Reuters reports thousands of people have been evacuated and some trains cancelled, a day before Cyclone Arnab's expected landfall.

22
00:02:26.375 --> 00:02:32.545
In Nigeria, Reuters reports authorities are tracking fifty three contacts linked to an Ebola patient.

23
00:02:32.545 --> 00:02:42.300
And in the West Bank, the U.N. humanitarian office says partners are supporting more than three thousand Palestinians evacuated from their homes in Hebron by Israeli forces.

24
00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:45.656
Now a few quick notes by region.

25
00:02:45.656 --> 00:02:49.440
In Africa, BBC Africa reports Algeria will send troops to Niger.

26
00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:56.885
In Somalia, journalist Harun Maruf reports heavy fighting yesterday between federal forces and al Shabaab near Leego.

27
00:02:56.885 --> 00:03:01.324
Al Shabaab claims it killed more than three hundred soldiers in an ambush there.

28
00:03:01.324 --> 00:03:05.204
That is a militant claim, and no official figure has been reported.

29
00:03:05.204 --> 00:03:19.945
In the Middle East, a drone strike on the Damascus to Homs highway in Syria yesterday killed three people, including Abu Abdul Rahman al Libi, a commander in the militant group Hurras al Din, a Syrian Defense Ministry source told A F P.

30
00:03:19.945 --> 00:03:26.586
In Iraq, the outlet Shafaq News reports a Baghdad court sentenced six French nationals to life in prison and a seventh to fifteen years for belonging to ISIS.

31
00:03:26.586 --> 00:03:37.163
And the Institute for the Study of War and the Critical Threats Project report officials from Mecca Pact countries met in Tehran yesterday.

32
00:03:37.163 --> 00:03:49.172
In Europe, Reuters reports a Russian missile strike on Kyiv yesterday killed at least one person and injured ten, including students at a university dormitory, and Russian strikes on Kharkiv killed two.

33
00:03:49.172 --> 00:03:54.558
Radio Free Europe reports a humanitarian cease fire in Oleshky took effect early today.

34
00:03:54.558 --> 00:04:04.398
In Germany, journalist Florian Flade reports a German man was arrested at Frankfurt Airport on suspicion of trying to join the Islamic State in Somalia and Pakistan.

35
00:04:04.398 --> 00:04:08.141
And Australia's Smartraveller warns of protests in Spain.

36
00:04:08.141 --> 00:04:15.651
In South Asia, Dawn reports Pakistan's Balochistan government banned gatherings in Pishin district with immediate effect.

37
00:04:15.651 --> 00:04:25.311
On cyber, The Record reports the A I software project LiteLLM said a key accidentally exposed in May was behind last week's supply chain attack.

38
00:04:25.311 --> 00:04:26.709
That's today's brief.

39
00:04:26.709 --> 00:04:35.068
These security developments come from government travel advisories and trusted analysts, curated by the Concilium Security Risk Management Team.

40
00:04:35.068 --> 00:04:43.322
The brief summarizes public reporting and isn't a substitute for your own risk assessment, so check the original source before making travel decisions.

41
00:04:43.322 --> 00:04:45.426
This brief is digitally narrated.

42
00:04:45.426 --> 00:04:46.408
Questions?

43
00:04:46.408 --> 00:04:50.011
Reach Concilium at info at concilium dot U.S.

44
00:04:50.011 --> 00:04:52.130
Thanks for listening, and stay safe.
